From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 23:10:27 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 85/94] Plutonium: xdg_toplevel_icon_v1, apps' window icons for
 the shells

An app without a desktop entry, or with several windows of their own
(a browser's profiles), names its window's icon or gives its pixels.
Exo asks for 128 px; the pixels, copied from the square wl_shm buffers
when added, become a PNG data URL (the smallest at least 128 px, else
the biggest, scaled down to 128). The name and URL go with the window
(EmbeddedWindows::Info, the broker's WindowInfo, NativeWindowEntry's
iconName and icon) to the shells, which look the name up as they look
app icons up (the helper's), else show the pixels; the switcher's
window rows look the name up first.
